 against the Rust source. Every one was caught except two provably equivalent mutants (`as i64 as u32` vs `as i32 as u32`; and dropping the `EOF` break after `scan_time_stamp`, since the next scan then breaks instead). Notably, commenting out `restore_default_sigpipe()` **is** caught by the broken‑stdout test — that's the one place Rust's runtime would otherwise exit 0 where C dies from signal 13.\n\n`translation/ERRORS.md` records the verification, every candidate mismatch investigated (with measured C output for each), and the mutation results.\n\n## Phase D — completion gate\n- ✅ both programs build with no errors\n- ✅ every enumerated input produces identical stdout, stderr and exit status\n- ✅ `cargo test` passes in `translation/` (19 integration + 5 unit tests, in both debug and release)\n- ✅ no test is disabled, skipped or `#[ignore]`d\n- ✅ `c_src/` unmodified (`luggage.c` md5 `af14ebf9…`, mtime unchanged; only the untracked `build/` dir was added by cmake)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":129613,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":669,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da36df0a-d233-448f-8a9e-391fd8a61084","uuid":"f31b2931-f39c-4773-96c0-976406154e93","timestamp":"2026-08-27T19:46:08.638Z"}
